       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any condition or stage of treatment where that dose is indicated. Doses above the maximum add lactic acidosis risk and no extra glucose control. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and the reason you gave doesn't say why this patient needs it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO twice daily.\n- **Enter the order with a note** if you tell me the specific indication and the plan for monitoring, such as lactate, renal function, and pharmacist or attending co-sign. I'd still be uneasy about the dose, so I'd rather you check it with pharmacy first.\n- **Route it through pharmacy or the attending.** If the dose is truly intended, a pharmacist's verification or a formal override in your order-entry system is the safer way to do it.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
